WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.737
Let's talk about the prevalence
of mental health problems in Portugal.

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.327
Portugal is one of the European countries

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.597
with the highest prevalence
of mental health problems.

4
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.177
Recent studies indicate
that over a third of the adult

5
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.617
population shows symptoms
of anxiety or depression,

6
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.037
and many of these cases do not receive

7
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.890
adequate clinical
or psychological support.

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.708
These numbers are not just statistics.

9
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.702
Behind every percentage,
there are people in real distress.

10
00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:31.367
This distress often remains invisible,
not because it doesn't exist,

11
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.857
but because it goes unrecognised,
by the person or by those around them.

12
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.837
In this context, work plays
a particularly relevant role.

13
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.037
It can act as a protective
factor by offering structure,

14
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.149
purpose and a sense of belonging.

15
00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.133
However, it can also be a source
of pressure, burnout and exclusion.

16
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.247
The way we organise
and experience work therefore has

17
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:57.833
a very decisive influence
on our mental health.
